# keepwarm configuration.
#
#   cp config.env.example config.env
#
# config.env is gitignored, so your settings survive a `git pull`. Everything
# below is commented out and shows the default. Any setting can also be
# overridden for a single invocation with a KEEPWARM_ prefix:
#
#   KEEPWARM_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna ./keepwarm ping

# --- schedule -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Length of the Codex usage window, in hours. Only change this if OpenAI
# changes the window length.
#WINDOW_HOURS=5

# Minutes to wait past the window boundary before pinging, to absorb clock skew
# between this machine and OpenAI's servers. Every minute here is a minute of
# the fresh window you don't get to use, so keep it small. If pings come back
# LIMITED in the log, raise it to 5.
#SLACK_MINUTES=2

# Minute of the hour the cron job fires on. Re-run "./keepwarm install" after
# changing this.
#CRON_MINUTE=2

# --- the ping itself ----------------------------------------------------------

# Model used for the keepalive. Empty means whatever the CLI would pick on its
# own. The usage window is account-wide, so the model does not change what a
# ping opens - it only changes what the ping is billed at. Set a small model
# here if your plan weights them differently.
#MODEL=""

# The keepalive prompt. Codex has no equivalent of a replaceable system prompt,
# so the request carries its normal instructions and tool schemas whatever this
# says; a longer prompt just adds to that.
#PING_PROMPT="ping"

# Transient local failures (brief network trouble, a contended token refresh)
# are retried within the same run. Without this a single blip costs a whole hour
# of window, because the next attempt would otherwise be the next hourly tick.
# Rate limits are NOT retried - those mean the window genuinely hasn't expired.
#PING_ATTEMPTS=3
#PING_RETRY_DELAY=20

# Seconds before a hung ping is killed. A codex that cannot authenticate retries
# its connection for around 30 seconds before giving up, and a wedged one would
# otherwise hold the lock until the next tick.
#PING_TIMEOUT=120

# 1 = pass --ignore-user-config, so the ping ignores ~/.codex/config.toml: no
# MCP servers, no profile, no custom model provider. Set to 0 if you point Codex
# at a provider of your own - otherwise the ping goes to the default one
# instead of yours.
#IGNORE_USER_CONFIG=1

# --- behaviour ----------------------------------------------------------------

# 1 = if you were already using Codex after the window boundary, your own
# messages already opened the new window, so skip the ping and just record it.
# 0 = always ping on schedule.
#SKIP_IF_RECENTLY_ACTIVE=1

# Where Codex writes session rollouts; used for the activity check. keepwarm's
# own pings run with --ephemeral and write nothing here, so they can never be
# mistaken for your activity.
#ACTIVITY_DIR="$HOME/.codex/sessions"

# --- paths --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Leave empty to auto-detect. Auto-detection checks PATH first, then the copies
# bundled inside the VS Code / Cursor extensions, then the standalone
# installer's versioned directory under ~/.codex/packages (newest wins, so an
# update doesn't break the cron job), then ~/.local/bin, ~/.bun/bin,
# ~/.npm-global/bin, /usr/local/bin and /opt/homebrew/bin.
#CODEX_BIN=""

# Days of log history to keep.
#LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=30
